---
import { ARENA_LIST, activeLevels } from '../../data/benchmarkSpec';
import { formatAggregateScore } from '../../data/formatting';
import { guideExample } from '../../data/guide';
---
<section id="leaderboard" class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="leaderboard-title">
 <p class="step">02 · Two-minute orientation</p><h2 id="leaderboard-title">Read the leaderboard from evidence outward.</h2>
 <p>The leaderboard publishes results; it does not make your deployment decision. Search and filters narrow the rows, show-more controls reveal additional results, and price/efficiency views remain separate from canonical scores.</p>
 {guideExample ? <div class="live-example"><p class="live-label">Live example from canonical leaderboard data</p><div class="example-row"><span><small>Official rank</small><strong>#{guideExample.rank}</strong></span><span class="model"><small>Tested configuration</small><strong>{guideExample.name}</strong></span><span><small>Overall</small><strong>{formatAggregateScore(guideExample.score)}%</strong></span>{ARENA_LIST.map(arena => <span><small>{arena.shortName}</small><strong>{formatAggregateScore(guideExample.scores[arena.id])}%</strong></span>)}</div><p class="fine">This example updates when canonical benchmark data changes. Open its level results on the <a href="/#global-leaderboard">leaderboard</a>.</p></div> : <p class="notice">No globally qualified configuration is currently available. Use arena tables and coverage labels instead.</p>}
 <ol class="orientation"><li><strong>Name means configuration.</strong> Provider, base model, thinking setting, and tool-enabled variant can change the tested system. Do not treat variants as interchangeable.</li><li><strong>Rank follows the unrounded canonical score.</strong> Displayed decimals can look tied even when full precision differs; exact ties share rank.</li><li><strong>Overall is broad, not universal.</strong> It is the equal mean across {ARENA_LIST.length} qualified arenas.</li><li><strong>Arena scores answer narrower questions.</strong> Inspect {ARENA_LIST.map(a=>a.name).join(', ')} according to your task.</li><li><strong>Levels show the failure shape.</strong> Active levels currently number {ARENA_LIST.map(a=>`${activeLevels(a).length} in ${a.shortName}`).join(', ')}.</li><li><strong>Coverage and PROVISIONAL qualify the number.</strong> Release date identifies the model release, not necessarily the evaluation date.</li></ol>
</section>
